{"availability":"available","full":"arthuralbefaro/relay","name":"relay","description":"Visual automation engine whose execution core runs unchanged in the browser and on a server. C# nodes compile to WebAssembly for the live demo and run behind ASP.NET in production, with shared golden fixtures keeping both in sync.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-16T17:25:22Z","updated":"2026-09-18T16:40:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://arthuralbefaro.github.io/relay/","topics":["aspnet","automation","bullmq","csharp","docker","dotnet","drizzle-orm","monorepo","nestjs","nextjs","pglite","postgres","react-flow","typescript","webassembly","workflow-engine"],"demo":"https://arthuralbefaro.github.io/relay/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.610Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.610Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.610Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.610Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Relay is a visual automation engine. You wire nodes on a canvas, run the flow, and inspect every attempt of every step. The same flow definition runs in two very different places without being rewritten: entirely inside the browser, or on a server behind a queue and a pool of workers.","Some nodes are written in C#. In the browser they run as WebAssembly; on the server the same assembly runs behind an ASP.NET service. One set of golden fixtures runs against both, so the two runtimes cannot drift apart without a test going red.","Other nodes call a language model. The demo answers from recorded text so that it works with no key at all, and you can paste your own Anthropic key to see real answers. The key stays in your tab and never reaches a Relay server."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/arthuralbefaro/relay/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ec63d703a63defd1054f18e1